  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-14, in chat): \"the slot operation should be possible to extend outside the face or edge selected in the direction of its length.\"\n\nWhat happens: a Slot operation cuts only the length of the selected face or edge. The user cannot extend the cut past the ends of the selection.\n\nExpected:\n- The Slot operation has an extension parameter for each end of the slot, along the length of the slot.\n- With an extension, the tool moves past the end of the selected face or edge by that distance. The default is no extension.\n- The extension follows the direction of the slot at that end.\n\nSafety: an extension changes the toolpath. The gouge check must judge the extended moves, and an extension into a part must stop the post.\n\nDone means: the Slot operation has the extension parameters, set through the undoable parameter command and the MCP tool `edit_operation`; a toolpath test pins that the pass extends by the given distance at each end; a test pins that an extension into a part is refused; the default output of existing Slot programs does not change.\n",
